3. Key Concepts & Warnings
 * Why __str__ Matters: Without __str__, printing an object outputs unhelpful default text like <__main__.Lathe object at 0x7f3a2c1b40> (the memory location). __str__ replaces this with a clean, human-readable nameplate.
 * Warning About __del__:
   * Writing del L1 removes the variable name reference. Python decides when to actually destroy the object and trigger __del__ (when no names point to it remaining).
   * __del__ is fine for log lines or general cleanup, but for critical precise moments (e.g., closing files, releasing resources), use a with block instead.
